  "method": "Fresh equivalent Chromium touch contexts. The second pair first taps an ordinary heading. Event listeners record trusted input and focus modality. The observational focus wrapper delegates to the original method with unchanged arguments. No focus or navigation behaviour is replaced.",
  "finding": "The protected tab receives native touch focus without a keyboard focus ring. Tabs 1.2.1 explicitly focuses inside mouse-down, so the resulting focus event has no touch source capability and matches focus-visible. The full final discovery gate retains strict touch focus equality.",
